WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:04.680
December's almost here, Santa Claus will be
taking to the skies, and he won't be alone:

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:08.120
Along with the reindeer doing all the work
pulling his sleigh, the skies are going to

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:12.100
be crowded with spaceships and balloons thanks
to Amazon Prime Video.

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:17.520
For most movie fans, Felicity Jones is likely
best remembered as the reluctant hero Jyn

00:00:17.539 --> 00:00:20.869
Erso in 2016's Rogue One: A Star Wars Story.

00:00:20.869 --> 00:00:25.019
On December 6, she'll be taking a trip back
to the 19th century to become a pilot in the

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:26.720
Amazon original film The Aeronauts.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.480
Jones plays daredevil pilot Amelia Wren.

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:34.520
Accompanied by James Glaisher, played by Eddie
Redmayne, Wren takes to the sky via balloon

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:36.620
in hopes of making new discoveries in the
clouds.

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:40.840
The pair run into trouble on one of their
airborne journeys and, rather than discovering

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:43.500
new science, they find themselves in a fight
to survive.

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:47.400
The Aeronauts is fiction, but boasts some
solid footing in actual history.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:52.080
While Wren is a purely fictional character,
James Glaisher was a real meteorologist working

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:53.000
in the 19th century.

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:58.470
Based on the bestselling series of novels
by Daniel Abraham and Ty Franck, The Expanse

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:01.800
premiered on Syfy to critical and commercial
success in 2015.

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:07.060
The series follows a crew of antiheroes who
uncover a vast conspiracy during a time when

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:08.760
humanity has colonized the stars.

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:13.900
Unfortunately, Syfy announced The Expanse's
third season would be its last in May 2018.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:18.460
Thankfully for fans, Amazon Prime Video stepped
up to give the acclaimed series a new home.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:22.640
The show's third season ended with the crew
of the Rocinante traveling through the Ring

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:24.660
Gate to an entirely new region of space.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:28.240
All the surviving characters of the previous
season will be returning, but The Expanse

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:30.100
will have some new faces as well.

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:35.532
Lyndie Greenwood joins the cast as Dr. Elvin
Okoye, a UN scientist sent to explore a new

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:36.080
planet.

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:40.671
Burn Gorman will appear as Adolphus Murtry,
a man who wants to be the top dog on the new

00:01:40.671 --> 00:01:43.670
planet and doesn't care what he has to do
to make that happen.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:46.400
"Someday I think you and I are going to end
up bloody."

00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:51.760
Amazon Prime Video is bringing plenty of action
flicks to the streaming service in December,

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:53.800
including a couple that are more than meets
the eye.

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:57.940
When it comes to its superhero fare, Prime
Video is going outside the box.

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:03.369
As of Dec. 1, subscribers can watch 2008's
Hancock, in which Will Smith plays a deadbeat

00:02:03.369 --> 00:02:07.260
guy with Superman-like powers who has to figure
out how to be a genuine hero.

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:13.340
On December 11, subscribers can watch 2018's
Fast Color, starring Gugu Mbatha-Raw as a

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:16.700
young homeless woman with emerging powers
she hasn't learned to control.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:21.000
Don't expect this to be the last you see of
Fast Color on Amazon, either: In July 2019,

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:25.680
it was announced Amazon Studios is developing
an original series based on the film.

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:30.900
If you're eager for robot action, you'll be
able to stream 2018's Bumblebee starring Hailee

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:35.060
Steinfeld, Jorge Lendeborg Jr., and wrestler
John Cena on December 13.

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:40.160
Finally, on Dec. 30, Amazon will stream 2011's
action-packed Transformers: Dark of the Moon.

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:45.740
If you prefer your entertainment on the more
thrilling and terrifying side of things, Amazon

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:48.500
Prime Video has some new offerings in December
that might pique your interest.

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:53.660
On December 1, you can watch Denzel Washington
as tries to solve a murder before he becomes

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:56.280
the prime suspect in 2003's Out of Time.

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:00.750
That same day, the service will also offer
a couple of corny '70s horror flicks that

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:01.820
insect lovers should adore.

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:07.440
There's 1974's Phase IV, featuring an army
of sentient ants waging war on a desert's

00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:08.100
human inhabitants.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:14.090
And don't forget 1975's Bug, in which California
earthquakes unleash foot-long cockroaches

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:16.180
on the peaceful California city of Riverside.

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:20.820
On the ninth, watch Casey Affleck and Elisabeth
Moss struggle to survive a dying world in

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:22.660
the post-apocalyptic thriller Light of My
Life.

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:26.660
On Christmas Day, Prime Video begins streaming
2018's Night Hunter.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:31.560
The psychological thriller stars Henry Cavill
as weathered Detective Walter Marshall tracking

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:33.640
down a serial killer that targets young women.

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:38.520
Ben Kingsley appears as a former judge turned
vigilante who's launching his own investigations,

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:43.080
while Alexandra Daddario] stars as criminal
profiler Rachel Chase.

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:44.900
Looking for a little drama?

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:49.610
On the first of the month, you can check out
2000's Almost Famous, which follows a teenager

00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:53.830
who gets tapped to tour with the fictional
rock band Stillwater and write about the experience

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:55.000
for Rolling Stone magazine.

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:58.600
Plus, there's the 1987 John Hughes classic
Some Kind of Wonderful.

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:02.840
After that, you can cut loose and show your
rebellious dancing side by watching the 1984

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:04.020
hit Footloose.

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:09.200
Finally, you can watch Leonardo DiCaprio become
the legendary Howard Hughes in 2004's The

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:09.760
Aviator.

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:15.239
Amazon Prime Video is a little light on comedy
offerings in December, but its new arrivals

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:18.540
include one impressive standout – 1999's
Man on the Moon.

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:23.620
The biopic about the late Andy Kaufman is
named after the REM single "Man on the Moon,"

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:25.740
which paid tribute to the unorthodox comedian.

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:29.880
Jim Carrey plays Kaufman, in a performance
that saw him staying in character for much

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:32.240
of the film's production, both on and off
set.

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:36.460
Carrey won a Golden Globe for his efforts
and the film is largely regarded as the moment

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:39.620
any doubts that Carrey could excel as a "serious"
actor were dispelled.

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:44.080
While the actor made his bones playing absolutely
ridiculous characters like the lead of The

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:48.690
Mask and the Ace Ventura: Pet Detective films,
Carrey made great strides in the late 90s

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:49.780
to broaden his horizons.

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:54.860
His portrayal of a man who doesn't know he's
the subject of a lifelong reality series in

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:59.720
1998's The Truman Show convinced many moviegoers
Carrey could do more than straight comedy,

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:02.000
and Man on the Moon convinced many of the
stragglers.

